# Copy to `.dev.vars` (gitignored) for local development. Wrangler loads it automatically.
# Local development needs nothing here: the mock email provider needs no credentials and a
# fixed development-only signing secret is used when AUTH_HMAC_SECRET is unset.
# Non-secret settings live in wrangler.jsonc `vars`; put only secrets and local overrides here.

# Local override examples:
# LOG_LEVEL=debug
# APP_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173

# Secrets. Never commit real values. In staging/production set them with
# `wrangler secret put <NAME> --env <staging|production>`, never in wrangler.jsonc.
# AUTH_HMAC_SECRET: >= 32 random chars; signs login codes, session tokens and throttle keys.
#   Generate one with:  node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('base64url'))"
#   Rotating it signs everyone out and invalidates pending codes (no data is lost).
# AUTH_HMAC_SECRET=
# EMAIL_PROVIDER_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=
